n record-only, consistent with the banner), or add a short current install section against /opt/arrt-player and point README.md at it.", "files": ["deploy/README.md", "README.md"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "deploy/README.md opening second blockquote begins mid-sentence", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: the blockquote at lines 23-28 opens with '> server on the NAS** (\u00a7 The Player as a client of the NAS, below). Its `curation.service` is stopped\u2026' - its first line(s), including the opening of the bold span, were lost when the monorepo text was trimmed (present since bae7e10), so 'Its' has no referent and the rendered Markdown carries a stray `**`. Restore the opening clause from Arrt's copy or delete the fragment; the banner above already says what the dated sections are.", "files": ["deploy/README.md"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "Prose carried from Arrt describes Arrt's tree, not this one", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: guards and config were carried from the monorepo with their justifying prose intact, and that prose names things that do not exist here. Sites found: .github/scripts/assert_tests_ran.py docstring (browser.yml, the live probes, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, dezoomify-rs, 'the curation suite carries one xfail'); tests/test_assert_tests_ran.py `test_every_ci_pytest_invocation_scopes_a_path` docstring ('Five suites here are deselected by a marker expression in `addopts` - the browser one and the four live/eval ones' - this pyproject's addopts has none; `api-drift.yml` 'does'; 'CLAUDE.md and docs/testing.md \u2026 cd arrt && uv run pytest') and `_ci_pytest_invocations` ('`api-drift.yml` does'); pyproject.toml ('the reason the two planes are sibling uv projects rather than one workspace', 'The same strict set the curation plane carries'); suites.yml typesetting comment ('Folding these into the display leg' - no such leg); tests/test_norm_index.py docstring ('across every plane's config', plus a dated narration of what an earlier version said, which is a deletion case). None is read by a test or gate, so this is NOTE and no fix commit is wanted for it alone; when these files are next touched, delete the Arrt-specific claims or make them relational. For assert_tests_ran.py specifically, the pyproject per-file-ignores comment records a deliberate byte-for-byte copy 'so the two copies can be compared by diff' - that choice is what keeps the false prose here, and nothing mechanizes the diff it promises; either let the copy diverge and correct the docstring, or keep it verbatim and say in its docstring that the named workflows are Arrt's. Search to bound the class: grep the subject files for curation|browser|api-drift|live_|OPENROUTER|dezoomify|workspace|plane|cd arrt.", "files": [".github/scripts/assert_tests_ran.py", "tests/test_assert_tests_ran.py", "pyproject.toml", ".github/workflows/suites.yml", "tests/test_norm_index.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "blocking", "title": "The runbook deploy/README sends the operator to for the move still drives the monorepo checkout, and its commands fail against this repository", "recommendation": "Records Pass, 'must stop the merge' bar (wrong commands). deploy/README.md's preamble says that from 2026-10-26 display.service names a checkout at /opt/arrt-player with .env at its root, and that 'Moving the Pi onto that checkout is .prawduct/runbooks/moving-the-pi-player-to-a-new-revision.md'. That runbook still uses the monorepo layout throughout. Steps 5-6 fetch and check out `<new>` in /opt/samsung-frame-art-loader, whose origin is Arrt, so a commit made only in this repo is not there. Step 8 runs `cd /opt/samsung-frame-art-loader/arrt-player && uv sync`, a subdirectory a stand-alone checkout does not have. Step 7 edits /opt/samsung-frame-art-loader/.env, not the /opt/arrt-player/.env the new unit reads. 